{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": "Solving Problems"}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "In the Supply Room"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 5}, {"type": "level", "content": "Beginner"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " There Is and There Are with Some, Any and A Lot Of"}, {"type": "describer", "content": " "}, {"type": "example", "content": "There are some cups on the table."}, {"type": "text", "content": "In sentences that introduce things, you use <span class=\"strong\">there is</span> (for singular) <br />or <span class=\"strong\">there are</span> (for plural)."}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":\"3\",\"columns\":\"2\",\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\">With Count Nouns <br /> (books)</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<span class=\\\"strong\\\"> With Non-count Nouns<br /> (water)</span>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"There <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> are </span>  some ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"There <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> is </span>  some ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"There <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> aren't </span>  any ...\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"There <span class=\\\"strong\\\"> isn't </span>  any ...\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" instruction_table_background intro_table_border\"}"}, {"type": "example", "content": " There isn't any coffee."}, {"type": "text", "content": "With count nouns you use a plural verb.<br /><span class=\"strong\"> some </span> = a small number <span class=\"italic\"> &nbsp &nbsp <br /> Example: There are some pens. </span><br /><span class=\"strong\"> not any </span> =  zero <span class=\"italic\"> &nbsp &nbsp <br /> Example: There aren't any pens. </span></span><br />"}, {"type": "text", "content": "With non-count nouns you use a singular verb.<br /><sn class=\"strong\"> some </span> =  a small amount <span class=\"italic\"> &nbsp &nbsp <br />Example: There is some coffee.<br /></span><span class=\"strong\">not any</span> </span> = zero <span class=\"italic\"> &nbsp &nbsp <br />Example: There isn't any coffee. </span><br /></span><br />"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": " Asking Someone to Hand You Something in a Polite Way"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use polite language to ask a person to hand you something at work. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Ashley</span>: Could you please hand me the stapler? <br /> <span class=\"strong\">Bruce</span>: Here you are. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Use <span class=\"italic\">Could you please + action ... ? </span> <br /> Use a polite answer like <span class=\"italic\"> Here you are. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Amanda</span>:  Could you please give me the book? <br /> <span class=\"strong\">Bart</span>: Yes, here you are."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "to check"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to look carefully"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Let's check the supplies."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le05ob03aud06"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear at work."}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "binder"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a cover for paper"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: There is some paper in my school binder."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "engenn1le05ob03aud01"}]}, {"type": "target_word"